iption_full":"Pasqal Holding SA develops neutral-atom quantum computers and provides a full-stack quantum computing platform. The company designs and manufactures quantum processors based on neutral-atom technology and integrates them with high-performance computing environments for hybrid quantum computing applications. Its platform includes quantum hardware, programming, and simulation tools, such as Pulser and Pulser Studio; and cloud-based access that enables users to develop, test, and run quantum algorithms remotely. The company also develops quantum software tools, developer SDKs, emulation capabilities, and cloud services through its Pasqal compute platform to support quantum application development. In addition, it provides consulting, training, and collaborative development of quantum algorithms and applications for various industries, including finance, energy, healthcare, and logistics. Pasqal Holding SA is based in Palaiseau, France.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Wasiq  Bokhari Ph.D. | CEO & Executive Chairman","financial_summary":["Pasqal Holding SA is a small-cap technology business with a $794M market cap on $19M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +430% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -94% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 81% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $41M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -11.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 4.6% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 59% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 52% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Beneish M-Score flags potential earnings manipulation \u2014 a question of whether the reported numbers can be trusted","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"SGA costs surged 39% YoY \u2014 may reflect legal, restructuring, or operational issues","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 311% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Technology peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Gross margin tops the Technology peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Growing faster than most Technology peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Pasqal (NASDAQ:PSQL) Shares Down 9.2% \u2013 What\u2019s Next?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"ht